  "limitations": [
    "One top-level pair of manual approval then unbound literal native checkout branches with failFast false. Each checkout uses an identity-derived relative directory.",
    "The observer controls approval order and observes branch completion, native directory ownership, marker contents, join and original rejection. This does not prove simultaneous CPU or Git activity.",
    "Only branch-local checkout directories are certified: no workspace export, artifact transfer, state continuity, security boundary, clean-directory guarantee or cross-build isolation.",
    "No failFast-true checkout bodies, nested or arbitrary branch work, human authorization, public support promotion or portable execution. The disposable runtime host and observer remain trusted."
  ]
}
